     Looking through the executable, I noted that there was a string for
"There is something written here in a very strange way."  I wonder what the
stats are for that method of writing (obviously, it's an error report and
you should never see it, but it'd be interesting)....
     If something is "burned into the floor" will it last longer than an
engraving (a la athame or wand of digging)?  That could make wands of light-
ning useful (if you were blindfolded).
     Oh yes.  A pet peeve-- if you're blinded and have telepathy, "it hits"
and "you hit it" are inappropriate, since you can identify monsters with the
/ command.

     Now for the long-standing bug (this might even be big enough to change
in pl8, but that might be too risky):
     When a rust monster or dwarf eats away at the edges of a room, the
square turns blank instead of to a doorway symbol.  When it eats away at a
passage next to you (edge of room or just rock), the square also turns blank,
and you must either move onto the square or move away from the square and back
onto another square next to it before it registers as passageway.  Notably,
whenever one moves onto the border of a room, all of the changed squares
register as being doorways.
     Dwarves dig with pickaxes, right?  Why don't you (the player) generate
rocks and boulders when digging with a pickaxe?  Why can dwarves dig through
a wall in one turn?  Why *can't* the player when he's polymorphed into a rock
mole?  And, if you pickpocket the dwarf as a nymph (which I haven't tried,
so I don't know if it's possible) so it doesn't have its pickaxe, can it still
dig through walls?  How?
     And shouldn't peaceful dwarves refrain from doing a furniture 
rearrangement on the level?  I get tired of trying to get my dog to kill those
pests.

